1
00:00:06,820 --> 00:00:12,060
=Fatal Proximity to Him=

2
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:14,100
=Episode 7=

3
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:17,180
Tomorrow's your birthday.

4
00:00:17,180 --> 00:00:18,780
You're not celebrating again this year?

5
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:21,260
I've always felt like my birthday

6
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:22,460
is kind of cursed.

7
00:00:22,540 --> 00:00:24,700
Something always seems to happen.

8
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:31,100
(Admission Notice)

9
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:32,420
An admission notice!

10
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:37,140
(Academic Exam Admission Notice
Luo Xiyu, Ranked No. 1 Nationwide)

11
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:37,820
Nationwide...

12
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:39,180
Number one nationwide?

13
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:39,700
Calm down.

14
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:40,860
I can't calm down!

15
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:42,180
This isn't just your victory.

16
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:43,340
It's a victory for all of us!

17
00:00:44,380 --> 00:00:45,140
Everyone!

18
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:46,540
Tomorrow is Xiyu's birthday.

19
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:48,220
To celebrate both pieces of good news,

20
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:48,780
I hereby declare

21
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:49,540
that tomorrow we're all going out

22
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:50,300
for barbecue!

23
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:51,300
Zhang Jinghang's treat!

24
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:53,420
Yeah!

25
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:56,340
You really don't have to.

26
00:00:56,340 --> 00:00:57,340
This is worth celebrating.

27
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:58,260
Everyone,

28
00:00:58,460 --> 00:00:59,900
we're all happy for Xiyu,

29
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:00,780
right?

30
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:01,700
Right!

31
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:03,820
All hail Xiyu!

32
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:18,700
(A Brief History of Time)

33
00:01:20,060 --> 00:01:22,140
(I hope this time I can change my fate)

34
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:23,780
(and not die young again.)

35
00:01:28,420 --> 00:01:29,780
Happy birthday.

36
00:01:29,780 --> 00:01:30,700
Thanks.

37
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:31,820
Happy birthday.

38
00:01:31,820 --> 00:01:32,300
Thank you.

39
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:32,980
Happy birthday.

40
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:34,220
Thank you.

41
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:36,980
Xiyu,

42
00:01:37,460 --> 00:01:37,940
happy birthday.

43
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:41,100
What a beautiful music box.

44
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:43,060
Xiyu,

45
00:01:43,380 --> 00:01:44,340
when you dance,

46
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:45,700
you're more precious than crystal.

47
00:01:46,060 --> 00:01:46,980
Thank you for the gift.

48
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:47,900
I love it.

49
00:01:47,980 --> 00:01:49,660
Now that's a meaningful gift.

50
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:51,460
No wonder you're the class monitor.

51
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:55,100
Every gift means a lot.

52
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:56,300
It's the thought that counts.

53
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:57,700
Enough with the sentimental stuff.

54
00:01:57,820 --> 00:01:59,300
One more grilled fish, please!

55
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:01,300
Since when are you shy
about ordering food?

56
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:02,820
Mind your own plate.

57
00:02:02,820 --> 00:02:03,500
Alright now.

58
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:04,100
Let's cut the cake.

59
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:05,140
Come on, cake time.

60
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:05,700
Okay.

61
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:07,020
Birthday girl

62
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:08,740
gets the first slice.

63
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:14,940
Ma'am?

64
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:16,860
Ma'am!

65
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:23,860
Didn't we already arrange
this yesterday?

66
00:02:24,380 --> 00:02:25,780
I've been waiting twenty minutes.

67
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:27,460
Sorry.

68
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:29,620
Your shoes are custom-made by hand.

69
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:30,820
The leather for the toe just arrived,

70
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:32,340
and the craftsman is working
on them now.

71
00:02:32,420 --> 00:02:33,500
Please give us a moment.

72
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:35,060
Just a moment.

73
00:02:41,460 --> 00:02:42,580
You know what?

74
00:02:42,860 --> 00:02:44,700
Song Shuqi got her
academic exam certificate too.

75
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:46,300
But she ranked twenty-second.

76
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:47,620
Way behind you.

77
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:50,820
Twenty-second still gives her
a pretty good chance of getting in.

78
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:52,140
What?

79
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:55,660
Don't tell me you'll end up
in the same class in college too.

80
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:57,380
What terrible luck.

81
00:02:57,620 --> 00:02:58,340
Seriously, the worst.

82
00:02:59,140 --> 00:03:00,140
Life is so unfair.

83
00:03:01,980 --> 00:03:02,780
Actually,

84
00:03:03,460 --> 00:03:04,460
she's a pretty good dancer.

85
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:06,860
If she focused more on herself,

86
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:08,540
she'd probably do even better.

87
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:16,260
(He Lan: I'm waiting in the warehouse
behind the billiards hall.)

88
00:03:16,660 --> 00:03:18,060
(I have something important
to tell you.)

89
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:27,540
He Lan?

90
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:36,580
Why are you here?

91
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:39,980
Happy birthday to you.

92
00:03:40,580 --> 00:03:42,180
Happy birthday, witch.

93
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:44,420
You like playing hide-and-seek, huh?

94
00:03:44,940 --> 00:03:45,900
Better hide well.

95
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:47,380
I'll take my time finding you.

96
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:01,140
Isn't that the blond punk
who's always with Li Junsheng?

97
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:03,260
Why's he hanging around here?

98
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:08,220
Ma'am,

99
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:09,180
how much longer?

100
00:04:10,140 --> 00:04:11,220
Just a little longer.

101
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:13,540
If there's anything in the shop
you want to...

102
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:14,660
Do you know that guy outside?

103
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:14,940
Huh?

104
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:15,580
No.

105
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:16,460
No?

106
00:04:18,580 --> 00:04:19,660
Are my shoes ready?

107
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:21,140
Your shoes...

108
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,380
I'm asking you one last time.

109
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:27,860
Are my shoes already finished?

110
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:29,700
No, I...

111
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:30,980
That blond guy...

112
00:04:30,980 --> 00:04:31,860
He threatened me.

113
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:33,380
He told me to stall you, or he'd...

114
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:40,300
What did Li Junsheng send you here
to do?

115
00:04:40,460 --> 00:04:41,660
I don't know what you're talking about.

116
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:42,700
You don't?

117
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:45,500
Okay! Fine!

118
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:46,300
I'll talk!

119
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:47,860
He told me to keep you here.

120
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:49,100
He took your phone.

121
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:51,500
Where is he?

122
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:52,940
At the billiards hall.

123
00:04:53,340 --> 00:04:54,340
In the warehouse out back.

124
00:05:03,140 --> 00:05:04,380
(Emergency Service)

125
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:05,660
Found you!

126
00:05:06,540 --> 00:05:07,900
I've never done anything to you.

127
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,260
Who sent you?

128
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:11,340
Someone

129
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:13,380
did ask me to teach you a lesson.

130
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:17,180
This is Sheng.

131
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:18,100
If you need anything,

132
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:19,380
just talk to him.

133
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:22,660
I want to teach this girl a lesson.

134
00:05:22,660 --> 00:05:23,700
Can you handle that?

135
00:05:23,940 --> 00:05:24,820
I'll pay you well.

136
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:33,780
Then you've definitely

137
00:05:33,780 --> 00:05:34,700
come to the right guy.

138
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:40,540
Yeah, run.

139
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:41,220
Keep running.

140
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:42,380
Faster.

141
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:43,300
Pick up the pace!

142
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:44,220
Keep running!

143
00:05:44,660 --> 00:05:44,940
That's it!

144
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:45,300
Don't stop!

145
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:46,780
Keep running!

146
00:05:49,220 --> 00:05:50,100
Listen,

147
00:05:50,460 --> 00:05:51,860
I'm better than He Lan.

148
00:05:51,940 --> 00:05:52,580
Give me a try.

149
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:54,020
You might even like it.

150
00:05:58,740 --> 00:05:59,940
Let go of me!

151
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:00,700
Let me go!

152
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:01,620
We've got plenty of time for this.

153
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:16,580
I'm sorry.

154
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:17,300
I'm late.

155
00:06:18,140 --> 00:06:19,100
Is he dead?

156
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:19,980
He's fine.

157
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:20,900
He's just unconscious.

158
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:21,460
He'll be okay.

159
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:22,300
You need to go.

160
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:23,780
Pretend none of this ever happened.

161
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:24,740
Remember, you were never here.

162
00:06:24,740 --> 00:06:25,740
What about you?

163
00:06:26,580 --> 00:06:27,260
I'll be fine.

164
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:28,700
He's my brother.

165
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:29,580
Nothing serious will happen.

166
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:30,780
Oh, right.

167
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:33,540
Take this.

168
00:06:34,580 --> 00:06:35,340
Happy birthday.

169
00:06:36,060 --> 00:06:36,620
Now go.

170
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:37,140
Hurry.

171
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:38,020
Go!

172
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:55,940
(He Lan, are you okay?)

173
00:07:09,260 --> 00:07:11,380
(Isn't this the ring
He Lan always wears?)

174
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:12,780
(How come it's here?)

175
00:07:14,740 --> 00:07:16,740
(It must've fallen into my bag
during that fight.)

176
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:18,900
(Now that I think about it,)

177
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:21,780
(I haven't gone to He Lan
to recharge in ages,)

178
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:23,540
(but I've still been full of energy
every day.)

179
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:26,540
(What if He Lan wasn't
the one charging me all along?)

180
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:28,060
(What if it was this ring?)

181
00:07:32,460 --> 00:07:34,060
(I wonder what happened yesterday)

182
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:36,060
(after he hurt his brother saving me.)

183
00:07:43,820 --> 00:07:44,380
(Composition Notebook)

184
00:07:47,260 --> 00:07:47,940
Zhang Jinghang.

185
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:53,140
This is half the money
for my dance lessons.

186
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:54,300
As for the rest,

187
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:55,980
I'll pay you back in installments.

188
00:07:56,580 --> 00:07:57,780
What dance lesson money?

189
00:07:58,260 --> 00:08:00,260
The twenty thousand
for my dance training.

190
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:03,020
Didn't you put it in my desk?

191
00:08:03,780 --> 00:08:04,620
That wasn't me.

192
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:05,860
I never put any money there.

193
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:13,420
Xiyu,

194
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:15,420
it was...

195
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:16,700
He Lan.

196
00:08:20,180 --> 00:08:21,300
I got to school early that day.

197
00:08:21,460 --> 00:08:24,220
I saw him put the money in your desk
with my own eyes.

198
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:28,380
Why didn't you tell me?

199
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:30,100
He Lan told me not to.

200
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:31,820
He said you didn't like him,

201
00:08:31,860 --> 00:08:33,180
and he didn't want to put pressure
on you.

202
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:34,740
What else do you know?

203
00:08:34,860 --> 00:08:35,860
Tell me everything.

204
00:08:36,060 --> 00:08:38,340
He said you wanted to go

205
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:38,980
to that lecture,

206
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:42,020
so he put a fake maintenance notice
on the bulletin board.

207
00:08:42,060 --> 00:08:43,060
To fake the official stamp,

208
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:46,100
he carved one out of a radish
and cut his hand doing it.

209
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:47,700
His wages from the billiards hall,

210
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:49,140
plus the money his grandma
left him for college...

211
00:08:49,140 --> 00:08:50,100
he gave all of it to you.

212
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:52,500
His brother fought him in the alley

213
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,020
because he wanted the money back.

214
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:55,060
And for your birthday,

215
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:56,940
he had dance shoes custom-made for you.

216
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:58,500
He even skipped breakfast to save money.

217
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:01,580
Xiyu,

218
00:09:02,020 --> 00:09:03,140
He Lan's been detained.

219
00:09:03,260 --> 00:09:04,500
He's in serious trouble this time.

220
00:09:04,780 --> 00:09:05,980
He hurt that guy badly.

221
00:09:06,260 --> 00:09:06,780
Apparently,

222
00:09:06,780 --> 00:09:08,220
there may be damage
to that guy's cerebellum.

223
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:09,820
He could have trouble walking
from now on.

224
00:09:10,180 --> 00:09:10,860
He Lan...

225
00:09:11,180 --> 00:09:11,980
might even

226
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:13,180
go to prison.

227
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:16,940
Xiyu, where are you going?

228
00:09:19,900 --> 00:09:20,820
What are you doing?

229
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:21,820
Ma'am,

230
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:23,660
if Li Junsheng can't go, then you go.

231
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:25,340
Go tell the police what really happened.

232
00:09:25,420 --> 00:09:27,100
That's not what happened at all.

233
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:28,540
Li Junsheng was trying to...

234
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:31,500
He was trying to assault me.

235
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:33,380
He Lan only hit him to protect me.

236
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:34,660
My son is hurt that badly,

237
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:36,460
and you're still trying
to smear his name?

238
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:38,340
You can't turn this around on us!

239
00:09:39,180 --> 00:09:41,180
Li Junsheng started all of this!

240
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:41,820
I...

241
00:09:41,820 --> 00:09:42,700
I'm telling you,

242
00:09:42,820 --> 00:09:44,100
He Lan already confessed.

243
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:45,420
He admitted he hurt him on purpose.

244
00:09:45,700 --> 00:09:46,540
I hope the judge

245
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:47,540
throws the book at him!

246
00:09:47,660 --> 00:09:48,140
He should

247
00:09:48,140 --> 00:09:49,300
stay in prison

248
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:50,260
and never come out.

249
00:09:50,820 --> 00:09:52,060
This is madness.

250
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,140
(Good Fortune)

251
00:10:17,140 --> 00:10:17,860
Who are you looking for?

252
00:10:17,940 --> 00:10:18,420
Sir,

253
00:10:18,860 --> 00:10:19,860
I'm He Lan's classmate.

254
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:20,900
He Lan is innocent.

255
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:21,740
Other people may not believe him,

256
00:10:21,740 --> 00:10:22,940
but you have to.

257
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:24,620
I'm his father.

258
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:26,420
Of course I want to believe him.

259
00:10:26,660 --> 00:10:28,220
But the police have already
reached their conclusion.

260
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,100
What can I do?

261
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:30,220
No, sir.

262
00:10:30,460 --> 00:10:31,700
Li Junsheng was trying to hurt me.

263
00:10:31,780 --> 00:10:33,180
He Lan only did it to protect me...

264
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:34,500
Girl,

265
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:36,500
I know you want to help He Lan.

266
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:37,580
I want to help him too.

267
00:10:37,820 --> 00:10:39,380
But you can't just make claims
like that.

268
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:40,260
That's enough.

269
00:10:40,660 --> 00:10:41,140
Sir!

270
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:41,940
Sir!

271
00:10:41,940 --> 00:10:42,960
Wait!

272
00:10:45,900 --> 00:10:46,540
Guess what

273
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:48,260
Li Xiaoxia said yesterday

274
00:10:48,260 --> 00:10:49,340
when I passed their house.

275
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:50,020
What?

276
00:10:50,580 --> 00:10:51,140
She said

277
00:10:51,140 --> 00:10:52,620
she couldn't control He Lan anymore.

278
00:10:52,940 --> 00:10:54,300
He keeps getting into trouble,

279
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:56,180
so she might as well let the police
handle him.

280
00:10:56,180 --> 00:10:57,220
Otherwise, the boy will only go astray.

281
00:10:57,900 --> 00:10:59,100
What did his dad say?

282
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:00,460
What do you think?

283
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:02,460
Once there's a stepmom,
the dad becomes a stranger too.

284
00:11:02,820 --> 00:11:03,460
He Lan

285
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:04,380
isn't a bad kid.

286
00:11:04,540 --> 00:11:05,500
His mom died when he was young,

287
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:06,540
so his grandma raised him.

288
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:07,580
After she passed away,

289
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:08,860
he came back to live with his dad.

290
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:10,860
Then that stepmother came along

291
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:12,020
and drove the poor kid to this.

292
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:13,340
And that son she brought with her?

293
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:15,100
You can tell he's bad news
just by looking at him.

294
00:11:15,380 --> 00:11:16,060
You're all

295
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:17,900
missing the real point.

296
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:20,180
Li Xiaoxia and her son

297
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:22,540
have had their eyes on
He Lan's grandma's old house

298
00:11:22,540 --> 00:11:23,380
for a long time.

299
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:24,500
I heard it's getting demolished.

300
00:11:24,900 --> 00:11:26,300
If He Lan really gets sent away

301
00:11:26,340 --> 00:11:28,700
for three or five years,

302
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:29,780
by the time he gets out,

303
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:30,820
there won't be a cent

304
00:11:30,860 --> 00:11:32,460
of the compensation money left for him.

305
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:33,980
That mother and son

306
00:11:34,020 --> 00:11:35,260
will have spent it all.

307
00:11:50,740 --> 00:11:54,300
(2014... 2025)

308
00:11:56,820 --> 00:11:58,500
(Do you know how many letters
I wrote you from prison?)

309
00:11:58,540 --> 00:11:59,700
(You never answered a single one.)

310
00:11:59,860 --> 00:12:00,540
(Luo Xiyu,)

311
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:01,820
(you really are heartless.)

312
00:12:02,140 --> 00:12:02,620
Buddy,

313
00:12:02,820 --> 00:12:04,100
about our schedule this afternoon...

314
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:05,100
Call me Mr. He from now on.

315
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:07,780
My brother will still be inside
for a while.

316
00:12:08,580 --> 00:12:10,380
Now that the company is in my hands,

317
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:11,860
we're going to do things by the book.

318
00:12:12,460 --> 00:12:13,660
We're making this a legitimate business.

319
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:14,820
Absolutely, Mr. He.

320
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:17,220
Tomorrow afternoon,

321
00:12:17,220 --> 00:12:18,780
we're attending the ribbon-cutting
at Yunshan Theater.

322
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:20,500
The real estate market
has been rough these past two years.

323
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:22,220
Construction on the theater
stalled halfway through.

324
00:12:22,420 --> 00:12:23,620
Yunshan took over the project,

325
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:24,300
and that's how

326
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:25,180
they finally got it finished.

327
00:12:25,860 --> 00:12:26,420
Starting this afternoon,

328
00:12:26,420 --> 00:12:27,500
it officially opens for performances.

329
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:29,220
What's showing?

330
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:30,180
It's

331
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:31,740
the Xinghai Ballet Company's production

332
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:32,740
of

333
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:33,820
Swan Lake.

334
00:12:33,900 --> 00:12:36,380
(Performance Schedule: 17:00
Xinghai Ballet Company: Swan Lake)

335
00:13:09,870 --> 00:13:14,750
♪I hide my racing heart without a sound♪

336
00:13:16,210 --> 00:13:21,010
♪I close my eyes and pretend
the story's been reset♪

337
00:13:22,330 --> 00:13:25,370
♪I steer clear of every path
that leads to you♪

338
00:13:25,370 --> 00:13:28,370
♪Trying to outrun the storm
we're destined for♪

339
00:13:28,890 --> 00:13:31,090
♪I thought if I didn't hear, see,
or speak of you♪

340
00:13:31,090 --> 00:13:34,530
♪I could cut every thread
that ties us together♪

341
00:13:35,770 --> 00:13:40,770
♪Through the endless night,
I guard my only secret♪

342
00:13:42,370 --> 00:13:47,370
♪In this new cycle, I watch you
become innocent again♪

343
00:13:48,530 --> 00:13:50,650
♪I tried to erase the fire we once had♪

344
00:13:50,650 --> 00:13:54,410
♪But I can't erase your name
carved into my bones♪

345
00:13:55,170 --> 00:13:57,370
♪The more I try to leave you behind♪

346
00:13:57,370 --> 00:14:01,610
♪The deeper I sink with no end in sight♪

347
00:14:01,610 --> 00:14:04,160
♪What if I stayed a little farther away♪

348
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:07,810
♪Could I finally break free
from this cycle♪

349
00:14:08,290 --> 00:14:10,170
♪What if I took things a little slower♪

350
00:14:10,170 --> 00:14:14,410
♪Could I delay the moment
everything falls apart♪

351
00:14:14,410 --> 00:14:18,210
♪Maybe if I retreat to the edge
of my dreams♪

352
00:14:18,210 --> 00:14:21,210
♪I could give you another future♪

353
00:14:21,530 --> 00:14:27,770
♪A tomorrow where I no longer exist♪

354
00:14:27,770 --> 00:14:30,010
♪Even if I never want to see you again♪

355
00:14:30,010 --> 00:14:31,650
♪This nightmare still won't end♪

356
00:14:31,650 --> 00:14:33,530
♪Even if it all plays out again♪

357
00:14:33,530 --> 00:14:35,730
♪I'll still find my way back to you♪

358
00:14:35,730 --> 00:14:39,610
♪Even if having you only leaves me
in your debt♪

359
00:14:39,610 --> 00:14:43,610
♪It's still better than
losing you forever♪
